-    python -I swg_tables.py roundtrip <file.iff|file.stf> [...]   # parse -> write -> compare bytes
-    python -I swg_tables.py show <file>                           # print the contents
-
-Formats
-  CSTB (misc/planet_crc_string_table.iff): FORM CSTB > FORM 0000 > DATA (count), CRCT (count x u32, ascending),
-       STRT (count x u32 offsets into STNG), STNG (zero-terminated names in CRC order). The CRC is the SOE table CRC:
-       MSB-first CRC-32, polynomial 0x04C11DB7, init 0xFFFFFFFF, final xor 0xFFFFFFFF (all 25 stock entries match).
-  DTII (datatables/**.iff): FORM DTII > FORM 0001 > COLS (count, names), TYPE (one type string per column, no count),
-       ROWS (count, then cells: 's' zero-terminated string, 'f' float32, anything else int32). Type strings may carry
-       a default after a bracket ("i[0]", "s[]"); only the first letter sets the cell size.
-  STF (string/**.stf): u32 0xABCD, u8 version (1), u32 next id, u32 count, then count x (u32 id, i32 crc (-1),
-       u32 length, UTF-16LE text) and count x (u32 id, u32 length, ASCII key).
